# Connect IQ build output.
#
# None of this is source. It is regenerated by barrelbuild / monkeyc on every
# build, and tracking it made every build dirty:
#
#   - external-mir/ unpacks the barrel into %TEMP% while compiling, so the
#     directory names embed an absolute temp path that differs per build.
#     That alone produced ~9000 lines of churn per build.
#   - bin/gen/ holds Rez.mcgen, regenerated from the resources each time.
#
# barrels.jungle points at BLE Barrel\BLE Barrel-1.0.0.barrel, so barrelbuild
# has to run before the apps are compiled. The VS Code extension does that on
# its own when the barrel is a project dependency.

# intermediate representations
mir/
internal-mir/
external-mir/
*.mir

# generated Rez sources and resource bundles
gen/
*.mcgen
*.mbc

# build products
*.barrel
*.barrel.debug.xml
*.prg
*.prg.debug.xml
*.iq

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]